    <h1>About My Community: Portland, Oregon
        Portland is a city defined by its relationship with geography and urban planning. As I prepare to move here on
        February 7, I am stepping into a "community of communities" known for its pioneering land-use laws and distinct
        "quadrant" system.

        The city is divided by the Willamette River and Burnside Street, creating a grid that prioritizes walkability
        and public transit. For someone arriving from the East Coast, the most striking aspect of this community is its
        "human-scale" design—short city blocks and a deliberate focus on preserving green spaces amidst dense
        urbanization. It is a city currently grappling with "disruptive uncertainty" in housing and livability, making
        it the perfect living laboratory for the CityLab Catalyst.

        </h1>
