    <p>Fieldwork Focus: The Central Eastside
        Reflections on the Community
        I have chosen to explore the Central Eastside for my fieldwork. This neighborhood is a fascinating collision of
        Portland’s industrial past and its "innovation" future. It is home to the "Electric Blocks"—a hub for tech and
        creative agencies—but it also remains a working industrial sanctuary.

        I chose this community because it embodies the "Waterfront Community" challenge:

        It sits directly on the river’s edge, making it vulnerable to climate shifts.

        It is experiencing rapid gentrification, pitting "emerging business opportunities" against the need for
        affordable housing and "social cohesion."

        As I move here on Feb 7, I want to understand how a neighborhood can maintain its gritty, productive soul while
        evolving into a modern, livable urban center.</p>

